Are you a man or a mouse? Farm Rodney. Summon Nasties doesn't respect
extinction. Even if were changed to respect extinction, you can just
kill Rodney.  One on one. Over and over again. Until you have seven
candles. Or fourteen.  Or eleventy-billion-and-one. I doubt anyone's 
fork/nerf/YANI/agonizingly stupid RGRN post is going to suggest making
it possible to get rid of Rodney permanently.

Nerfing pudding farming doesn't even prevent you from just farming the
first summoner you find. Surround an Archon with traps it won't cross
or something, wait for it to summon things, and kill them if you want.
Ad infinitum. What's that? It's harder than pudding farming? Well,
maybe it's closer to the right amount of challenge for the reward. So
sad? Too bad.

Worried you won't get an archon? You're guaranteed summoning monsters at
the Castle. If you can't get to the castle because there is no source of
digging or levitation or magical breathing or water walking or flying in
your entire game, and the guaranteed scrolls of earth you were going to
cross Medusa with vanished, and it isn't the Titan Medusa level (presto!
Summoner!), you can:

 * extinct everything easier until summoners get generated on the lowest 
   level you can get to, and farm those summoners
 * whistle or displace a pet into a polytrap until it turns into a summoner, 
   and then anger it
 * dip in fountains for a water demon and let demons hit you until one 
   summons a summoner (does Demogorgon summon? "that might resolve your 
   problem regardless")
 * Read the cursed book of the dead for arch-liches and farm them.

If you want a game you can't get yourself into an unwinnable situation in,
play Candy Land.[1] If you want to talk about unwinnable situations in
NetHack, why not start with accidental pre-Quest conversion or leaving
the Bell in the Quest and getting kicked out or getting disconnected at
the wrong time and having the portal on Earth not generated or something
that's based on a single mistake or error, not the RNG rolling a 1 on a
hundred-sided die a hundred billion times? Seriously. Right now, you can
still walk down the stairs at full health and get "The mumak butts! You
die..." You're making a problem up and arguing about fixing it when
there are way more interesting problems to solve in the same space.

There are legitimate arguments in favor of * farming that you could make.
People have made some of them. I feel they've been adequately refuted,
but you're welcome to disagree. You may not feel your argument to have
been adequately refuted, but I'm pretty sure that you're the only one who
feels that way; maybe your argument against some hypothetical nethack
where it's impossible to get items hasn't been refuted, but not even
Derek is suggesting that.

